From 51722b75c10f73d4afd69622f5108d3d2f4684d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: caoanhhao <caoanhhao@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 13:17:23 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] firmware: qcom: scm: allow qseecom on the Galaxy Tab S7 LTE

QSEE 0x1402000 on the SM-T875 answers app lookups (keymaster64,
qcom.tz.uefisecapp and tz_iccc run from the bootloader). Enable the
interface there so /dev/qseecom exists.

Starting an app from Linux does not work yet on this firmware: every
QSEOS_APP_START (smplap64, authhat, fingerpr, securefp, skm) returns SCM
status -2 with result 0xffffffd1 (-47), see docs/gts7l.md.

caoanhhao used AI to code
---
 drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
index 5b63ea559..624ac754a 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
@@ -2460,6 +2460,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id qcom_scm_qseecom_allowlist[] __maybe_unused = {
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,x1e80100-crd" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,x1e80100-qcp" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,x1p42100-crd" },
+	{ .compatible = "samsung,gts7l" },
 	{ }
 };
 
